member.summary:
Altitude above mean sea level in metres, sent in feet (/A=, rounded once to
            the foot), or in a Mic-E report in its altitude bytes, rounded to the metre (APRS12c ch. 10);
            one outside -10000 to 743570 m is refused there ().

A Mic-E position report, from  (APRS12c §10). The
position comment defaults to ; 
sets off alarms, so is only sent when asked for.

The APRS-IS q-construct in a packet's path, e.g. qAR,N3LLO-2: how the packet entered
APRS-IS and through which station or server (APRS12c §17 refers to the APRS-IS specification;
UAP §4). Present only on packets that came from APRS-IS.

The APRS-IS q-construct in a packet's path, e.g. qAR,N3LLO-2: how the packet entered
APRS-IS and through which station or server (APRS12c §17 refers to the APRS-IS specification;
UAP §4). Present only on packets that came from APRS-IS.

remarks.code:
AprsPacket packet = AprsStation.From("M0LTE-9").Via("WIDE1-1", "WIDE2-1")
    .Position(51.4543, -0.9781)
    .Symbol(AprsSymbol.Car)
    .CourseDegrees(88).SpeedKnots(36).AltitudeFeet(120)
    .Comment("Mobile")
    .Build();

AprsStation.From("M0LTE").Message("G3NRW", "Hi Ian").MessageId("01").Build();
AprsStation.From("M0LTE").Object("MYRPTR").At(51.45, -0.98).Symbol(AprsSymbol.Repeater)
    .Frequency(145.725, AprsToneType.Tone, toneValue: 118, offsetKHz: -600).Build();
AprsStation.From("M0LTE").Weather().At(51.45, -0.98).WindDirectionDegrees(220).WindSpeedMph(4)
    .WindGustMph(5).TemperatureFahrenheit(77).Build();
